    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6453" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cancĕrasco</span></b> , āvi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i> [cancer, III.], <i>to become
			cancerous</i>, <i>be afflicted with a cancer</i>, <i>to suppurate like a cancer</i> (post-class.; only
			in <i>perf.</i>), <i><span class="en">Plin. Val. 1,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. Horb. 36</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Marc. Emp. 9</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cancĕrātus</span></b> , a, um, <i>cancerous</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. Val. 4, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ulcera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 51</span></i>
			.</div>
